[{:db/id "q-75589/selection/8677255573c89f51bbda2655bf0990b3a6ef52dd073a8086551da4668a68282d" :answer/id #uuid "070a7758-3716-5b99-b438-d604be8b25ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75589/selection/6941cff48cebd9e4c9822110bc53fcdb7790ba04f618b331a0a8be09ff036b06" :answer/id #uuid "5a878ef1-ea20-5e0a-a290-00309d277797" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$v$ is not an eigenvector of $A$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75589/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "a1dc343e-6533-5d79-83a8-e4fb1462f063" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75589/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "1cc86d0c-6652-5585-8c8e-801a21c7fcae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75589/selection/3cdf72713560d0222db3f212ae773d6fe996b55e3f83de2fe203ec4142b4aac6" :answer/id #uuid "b59e3321-188d-5167-b2d0-db7db8656153" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{13}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75589/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "70547335-d416-5207-aba4-5d79c2b8d945" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75589/selection/6941cff48cebd9e4c9822110bc53fcdb7790ba04f618b331a0a8be09ff036b06" :answer-field/choices ["q-75589/selection/8677255573c89f51bbda2655bf0990b3a6ef52dd073a8086551da4668a68282d" "q-75589/selection/6941cff48cebd9e4c9822110bc53fcdb7790ba04f618b331a0a8be09ff036b06" "q-75589/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-75589/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-75589/selection/3cdf72713560d0222db3f212ae773d6fe996b55e3f83de2fe203ec4142b4aac6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75589" :question/id #uuid "700440da-12e4-50fe-86c5-d292870ad78e" :question/math-academy-id "q-75589" :question/problem "Determine if $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}].$\nIf so, then what is the corresponding eigenvalue?" :question/worked-solution "The eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $v$ is an eigenvector, then there must exist a real number $\\lambda $ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ Hence, we have\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]=\\lambda [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis leads to the following system of equations for $\\lambda :$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}11=3\\lambda  \\\\ 13=-2\\lambda \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis system has no solution. Therefore, $v$ is not an eigenvector of $A.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-75589/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4e9867f-15ba-5073-a20f-542045fced08"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75589"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70917/selection/6941cff48cebd9e4c9822110bc53fcdb7790ba04f618b331a0a8be09ff036b06" :answer/id #uuid "5952ab21-3b0c-50b9-913b-305ff7c06b67" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$v$ is not an eigenvector of $A$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70917/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "8c0f7913-f9a3-5e9c-9c60-430574c79c6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70917/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "09721ffc-5370-5014-9cba-533e43e4db02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70917/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "0e40e7bc-64dc-58df-8e7b-9aae720090bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70917/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "a2697a81-d07b-54e2-808d-a906b013899a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70917/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ee20386-319d-5f3f-9497-b8386be5dbc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70917/selection/6941cff48cebd9e4c9822110bc53fcdb7790ba04f618b331a0a8be09ff036b06" :answer-field/choices ["q-70917/selection/6941cff48cebd9e4c9822110bc53fcdb7790ba04f618b331a0a8be09ff036b06" "q-70917/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-70917/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-70917/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-70917/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70917" :question/id #uuid "740777a5-43a4-5203-8f0b-72f91859f44e" :question/math-academy-id "q-70917" :question/problem "Determine if $v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$\nIf so, then what is the corresponding eigenvalue?" :question/worked-solution "The eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $v$ is an eigenvector, then there must exist a real number $\\lambda $ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ Hence, we have\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=\\lambda [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis leads to the following system of equations for $\\lambda :$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2=2\\lambda  \\\\ 3=-\\lambda \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis system has no solution. Therefore, $v$ is not an eigenvector of $A.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-70917/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4e9867f-15ba-5073-a20f-542045fced08"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70917"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106744/selection/6941cff48cebd9e4c9822110bc53fcdb7790ba04f618b331a0a8be09ff036b06" :answer/id #uuid "c2eb3398-ae19-5ca2-ab18-d8935136c5e0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$v$ is not an eigenvector of $A$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106744/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "ae9a45ec-a2d4-5173-9908-784eaabd280e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106744/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "a60a30d1-8ebf-5d01-9942-d439f4339c66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106744/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "3a0b06b3-08a2-5110-ad50-78ebb74c0b61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106744/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "57a94b9a-0482-5936-b6e8-ad04da8947d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106744/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "34016eca-7fa9-5357-b97a-23860f2ff5c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106744/selection/6941cff48cebd9e4c9822110bc53fcdb7790ba04f618b331a0a8be09ff036b06" :answer-field/choices ["q-106744/selection/6941cff48cebd9e4c9822110bc53fcdb7790ba04f618b331a0a8be09ff036b06" "q-106744/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-106744/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-106744/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-106744/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106744" :question/id #uuid "b22af89b-1092-506b-925c-dc472e0f7d9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-106744" :question/problem "Determine if $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].$\nIf so, then what is the corresponding eigenvalue?" :question/worked-solution "The eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $v$ is an eigenvector, then there must exist a real number $\\lambda $ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ Hence, we have\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=\\lambda [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis leads to the following system of equations for $\\lambda :$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1=\\lambda  \\\\ -2=-\\lambda \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis system has no solution. Therefore, $v$ is not an eigenvector of $A.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106744/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4e9867f-15ba-5073-a20f-542045fced08"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106744"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-36791"] :question/problem "Determine if $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$  is an eigenvector of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nIf so, then what is the corresponding eigenvalue?" :question/worked-solution "The eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =5\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =5v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Av=5v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-107819/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "0aca831b-f409-5aa2-95e9-02ddde517ae6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107819/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "84c16fc6-7bd1-57e5-940a-387679a83103" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107819/selection/6941cff48cebd9e4c9822110bc53fcdb7790ba04f618b331a0a8be09ff036b06" :answer/id #uuid "f99a5d98-82ee-5fb8-84ea-cb3f5f274ed8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$v$ is not an eigenvector of $A$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107819/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "5c02a682-2a9c-5407-ac35-7dd5f73b0267" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107819/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "b94c8553-8d5e-59f2-9938-a9ffbb4d45d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107819/selection" :answer-fi