id #uuid "11c0fb27-de6d-5ff5-9bef-38221589ffdf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106828/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "83c8a6a6-00b3-5209-9404-fe4e49caa4e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106828/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "c3f88fe4-192b-567f-b245-562314735e70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106828/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e6080b57-b10d-5dd9-9f73-e2d70d0903f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106828/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-106828/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-106828/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-106828/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-106828/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-106828/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106828" :question/id #uuid "ea75fe73-8a8e-588a-8eaf-18860230f59a" :question/math-academy-id "q-106828" :question/problem "The eigenvector of $A=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ -k & -1\\end{aligned}]$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =k-1$ is  $[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =\\lambda v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ -k & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =(k-1)[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ -4k+4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4k-4 \\\\ -4k+4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-16=4k-4, \\\\ -4k+4=-4k+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for $k$ in the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n-12=4k\\,⟹\\,k=-3.\n$$\n\nThe second equation is true for any value of $k.$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the system is $k=-3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-106828/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7f5608f-a9f5-5e6a-b308-540ed8b29259"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106828"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75610/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "509d9686-b782-5098-8d44-67d9307adb25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75610/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "0a7a572b-76f3-5005-96a4-612f4632f248" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75610/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "f21a93e6-e6c6-52e5-8094-d37f812e5250" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75610/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "d8354623-60bd-5c96-b3ee-a96c0914763b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75610/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "f4fa832a-6af9-55f6-8d16-c29a44ab45e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75610/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cce53c32-fd8c-59de-8a66-cc917fff76c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75610/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-75610/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-75610/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-75610/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-75610/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-75610/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75610" :question/id #uuid "a7f901fa-248f-5ae5-86ed-bb1e2ea109ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-75610" :question/problem "An eigenvector of \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{aligned}]$ \ncorresponding to an eigenvalue $\\lambda =5k-4$ is $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3k-1\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =\\lambda v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3k-1\\end{aligned}] & =(5k-4)[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3k-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2+2(3k-1) \\\\ -10+8(3k-1)\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2(5k-4) \\\\ (5k-4)(3k-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}6k \\\\ 24k-18\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}10k-8 \\\\ 15{k}^{2}-17k+4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6k=10k-8 \\\\ 24k-18=15{k}^{2}-17k+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for $k$ in the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n6k=10k-8\\,⟹\\,k=2.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $k=2$ into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24k-18 & =15{k}^{2}-17k+4 \\\\ 24\\cdot 2-18 & =15\\cdot {2}^{2}-17\\cdot 2+4 \\\\ 30 & =30,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a true statement.\n\nTherefore, the solution of the system is $k=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-75610/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7f5608f-a9f5-5e6a-b308-540ed8b29259"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75610"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-18233/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "8e721d1c-2b5d-5774-b4d1-305b4f6f7273" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18233/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "07ce042c-ddf2-57a0-8e76-1832f4c73de4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18233/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "4b788941-acff-5edc-8fbc-6c557d5ffe45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18233/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "533ea0a8-594b-5a20-af3f-dda0eb6c2e7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18233/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "77f6ae69-73a4-5bcf-a824-96a0026a0c89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18233/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "965f540b-5be5-5b7a-9514-ee1681c35330" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-18233/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-18233/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-18233/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-18233/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-18233/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-18233/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-18233" :question/id #uuid "93364803-f932-5599-886a-b33bb951f95a" :question/math-academy-id "q-18233" :question/problem "An eigenvector of $D=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 10 \\\\ -7 & 11\\end{aligned}]$ corresponding to an eigenvalue $\\lambda =6$ is  $[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the eigenvectors of $D$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Dv=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Dv & =\\lambda v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-8 & 10 \\\\ -7 & 11\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}] & =6[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-8c+140 \\\\ -7c+154\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6c \\\\ 84\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-8c+140=6c \\\\ -7c+154=84\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Solving for $c$ in the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n-8c+140=6c\\,⟹\\,c=10.\n$$\n\n- Solving for $c$ in the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-7c+154=84\\,⟹\\,c=10.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the system is $c=10.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-18233/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7f5608f-a9f5-5e6a-b308-540ed8b29259"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-18233"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107837/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "6a18a2a3-5973-5132-8c42-b2a21fc869ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107837/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "4714ba84-bb14-5b1